    "result_text": "The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 2/2 tests passing). \n\n## Summary\n\nThe change is implemented following the codebase's existing pattern for derived owner attributes (like `locality`, `membershipLevel`, `membershipNumber`), where the logic lives as a computed getter on the `Owner` domain model and MapStruct maps it into the generated `OwnerDto` automatically.\n\n**Two edits:**\n\n1. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `getContactPreference()` getter that returns `\"EMAIL\"` when a non-empty email is present, otherwise `\"PHONE\"`. This puts the derivation right next to the `email` field it depends on, alongside the other derived getters, with single responsibility.\n\n2. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `contactPreference` property (read-only, enum `EMAIL`/`PHONE`) to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes the field and MapStruct wires it up. No controller, mapper, or copy-paste logic needed.\n\nBoth new acceptance tests (`corePhoneWhenNoEmail`, `functionalityEmailWhenPresent`) and the rest of the suite pass.",
